{"name":"Stucco Wall","hex":"#f1b19d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stucco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A material with binder and aggregate that is used to coat interior walls or to make interior mouldings.","A material with binder and aggregate that is used to coat exterior walls or to make exterior mouldings."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat or decorate with stucco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stucco"},{"term":"wall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rampart of earth, stones etc. built up for defensive purposes.","A structure built for defense surrounding a city, castle etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose with, or as if with, a wall or walls.","To use a wallhack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stucco","blocks":[{"text":"Stucco or render is a construction material made of aggregates, a binder, and water. Stucco is applied wet and hardens to a very dense solid. It is most commonly used as a decorative and protective cladding for exterior walls and canopies. Stucco can be applied over construction materials such as metal, expanded metal lath, concrete, cinder block, or clay brick and adobe for decorative, protective or structural purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Ceilings_of_the_rotonde_de_Mars_%28509%29.jpg/330px-Ceilings_of_the_rotonde_de_Mars_%28509%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stucco","wikidata":"Q33526"},{"title":"Wall","blocks":[{"text":"A wall is a structure and a surface that defines an area; carries a load; provides security, shelter, or soundproofing; or serves a decorative purpose. There are various types of walls, including border barriers between countries, brick walls, defensive walls in fortifications, and retaining walls that hold back dirt, stone, water, or noise. Walls can also be found in buildings, where they support roofs, floors, and ceilings, enclose spaces, and provide shelter and security."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg/330px-Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall","wikidata":"Q42948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Stucco_wall.jpg/500px-Stucco_wall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Stucco_wall.jpg/1280px-Stucco_wall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Stucco_wall.jpg/500px-Stucco_wall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stucco used as an exterior coating on a residential building.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStucco_wall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG/500px-Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG/1280px-Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG/500px-Stucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rock dash stucco used as an exterior coating on a house on Canada's west coast.  The chips of quartz, stone, and coloured glass measure approx. 3–6 mm (1/8–1/4\").","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStucco_rock_dash_-_detail.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik